      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Disclosure does not affect individual's liability for conduct.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Obligation persists regardless of disclosure."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-12a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12A Witnesses—immunity from liability etc.",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-12a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.25",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies to an individual (the witness) who provides\nassistance in relation to a public interest disclosure (other than the\nindividual who makes the disclosure), subject to section 12B.\nMeaning of provides assistance\n\n(2) A person provides assistance in relation to a public interest\ndisclosure if the person gives information or produces a document\nor other thing, or answers a question, that the person considers on\nreasonable grounds to be relevant to:\n\n(a) the making of a decision in relation to the allocation of a\ndisclosure under section 43; or\n\n(b) a disclosure investigation or a proposed disclosure\ninvestigation; or\n\n(c) a review or proposed review by the Ombudsman or the IGIS,\nunder subsection 55(3), about the handling of a disclosure.\nImmunity from civil, criminal or administrative action\n\n(3) The witness is not subject to any civil, criminal or administrative\nliability (including disciplinary action) because of the assistance\nprovided.\nImmunity from enforcement of remedies or rights\n\n(4) No contractual or other remedy may be enforced, and no\ncontractual or other right may be exercised, against the witness on\nthe basis of the assistance provided.",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies to an individual (the witness) who provides\nassistance in relation to a public interest disclosure (other than the\nindividual who makes the disclosure), subject to section 12B.\nMeaning of provides assistance\n\n(2) A person provides assistance in relation to a public interest\ndisclosure if the person gives information or produces a document\nor other thing, or answers a question, that the person considers on\nreasonable grounds to be relevant to:\n\n(a) the making of a decision in relation to the allocation of a\ndisclosure under section 43; or\n\n(b) a disclosure investigation or a proposed disclosure\ninvestigation; or\n\n(c) a review or proposed review by the Ombudsman or the IGIS,\nunder subsection 55(3), about the handling of a disclosure.\nImmunity from civil, criminal or administrative action\n\n(3) The witness is not subject to any civil, criminal or administrative\nliability (including disciplinary action) because of the assistance\nprovided.\nImmunity from enforcement of remedies or rights\n\n(4) No contractual or other remedy may be enforced, and no\ncontractual or other right may be exercised, against the witness on\nthe basis of the assistance provided.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-12a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-12a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-12a-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-12a-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-12a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12A Witnesses—immunity from liability etc.",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 25,
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies to an individual (the witness) who provides\nassistance in relation to a public interest disclosure (other than the\nindividual who makes the disclosure), subject to section 12B.\nMeaning of provides assistance\n\n(2) A person provides assistance in relation to a public interest\ndisclosure if the person gives information or produces a document\nor other thing, or answers a question, that the person considers on\nreasonable grounds to be relevant to:\n\n(a) the making of a decision in relation to the allocation of a\ndisclosure under section 43; or\n\n(b) a disclosure investigation or a proposed disclosure\ninvestigation; or\n\n(c) a review or proposed review by the Ombudsman or the IGIS,\nunder subsection 55(3), about the handling of a disclosure.\nImmunity from civil, criminal or administrative action\n\n(3) The witness is not subject to any civil, criminal or administrative\nliability (including disciplinary action) because of the assistance\nprovided.\nImmunity from enforcement of remedies or rights\n\n(4) No contractual or other remedy may be enforced, and no\ncontractual or other right may be exercised, against the witness on\nthe basis of the assistance provided."
    },
