    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-12a-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12A(2) Witnesses—immunity from liability etc.",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-12a-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.25",
      "values:originalText": "(2) A person provides assistance in relation to a public interest\ndisclosure if the person gives information or produces a document\nor other thing, or answers a question, that the person considers on\nreasonable grounds to be relevant to:\n\n(a) the making of a decision in relation to the allocation of a\ndisclosure under section 43; or\n\n(b) a disclosure investigation or a proposed disclosure\ninvestigation; or\n\n(c) a review or proposed review by the Ombudsman or the IGIS,\nunder subsection 55(3), about the handling of a disclosure.\nImmunity from civil, criminal or administrative action",
      "skos:definition": "(2) A person provides assistance in relation to a public interest\ndisclosure if the person gives information or produces a document\nor other thing, or answers a question, that the person considers on\nreasonable grounds to be relevant to:\n\n(a) the making of a decision in relation to the allocation of a\ndisclosure under section 43; or\n\n(b) a disclosure investigation or a proposed disclosure\ninvestigation; or\n\n(c) a review or proposed review by the Ombudsman or the IGIS,\nunder subsection 55(3), about the handling of a disclosure.\nImmunity from civil, criminal or administrative action",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-12a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-12a-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-12a-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fc2f444b67230f7770b205d2a8d21e6b6aecc2ca63b3678d2de44ff97ed9913b",
      "skos:note": "Immunity from civil, criminal or administrative action for providing assistance in relation to a public interest disclosure."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-12a-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12A(2) Witnesses—immunity from liability etc.",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 25,
      "values:originalText": "(2) A person provides assistance in relation to a public interest\ndisclosure if the person gives information or produces a document\nor other thing, or answers a question, that the person considers on\nreasonable grounds to be relevant to:\n\n(a) the making of a decision in relation to the allocation of a\ndisclosure under section 43; or\n\n(b) a disclosure investigation or a proposed disclosure\ninvestigation; or\n\n(c) a review or proposed review by the Ombudsman or the IGIS,\nunder subsection 55(3), about the handling of a disclosure.\nImmunity from civil, criminal or administrative action"
    },
