    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-12b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12B Witnesses—exceptions to immunities",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-12b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.26",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies to an individual (the witness) who provides\nassistance in relation to a public interest disclosure (other than the\nindividual who makes the disclosure).\nFalse or misleading statements etc.\n\n(2) Section 12A does not apply to the civil, criminal or administrative\nliability (including any disciplinary action) of the witness for\nknowingly making a statement that is false or misleading.\n\n(3) Without limiting subsection (2) of this section, section 12A does\nnot apply to the liability of the witness for an offence against\nsection 137.1, 137.2, 144.1 or 145.1 of the Criminal Code.\nDesignated publication restrictions\n\n(4) Section 12A does not apply to proceedings against the witness for\ncontravening a designated publication restriction.\nNote:\nFor designated publication restriction, see section 8.\nAssistance related to witness’ conduct\n\n(5) To avoid doubt, if the assistance provided relates to the witness’\nown conduct, section 12A does not affect the witness’ liability for\nthe conduct.\n\n\nProtection of disclosers and witnesses  Part 2\nProtections  Division 1\n\nSection 13\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nSubdivision B—Protection from reprisals",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies to an individual (the witness) who provides\nassistance in relation to a public interest disclosure (other than the\nindividual who makes the disclosure).\nFalse or misleading statements etc.\n\n(2) Section 12A does not apply to the civil, criminal or administrative\nliability (including any disciplinary action) of the witness for\nknowingly making a statement that is false or misleading.\n\n(3) Without limiting subsection (2) of this section, section 12A does\nnot apply to the liability of the witness for an offence against\nsection 137.1, 137.2, 144.1 or 145.1 of the Criminal Code.\nDesignated publication restrictions\n\n(4) Section 12A does not apply to proceedings against the witness for\ncontravening a designated publication restriction.\nNote:\nFor designated publication restriction, see section 8.\nAssistance related to witness’ conduct\n\n(5) To avoid doubt, if the assistance provided relates to the witness’\nown conduct, section 12A does not affect the witness’ liability for\nthe conduct.\n\n\nProtection of disclosers and witnesses  Part 2\nProtections  Division 1\n\nSection 13\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nSubdivision B—Protection from reprisals",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-12b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-12b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-12b-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-12b-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-12b-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-12b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12B Witnesses—exceptions to immunities",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 26,
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies to an individual (the witness) who provides\nassistance in relation to a public interest disclosure (other than the\nindividual who makes the disclosure).\nFalse or misleading statements etc.\n\n(2) Section 12A does not apply to the civil, criminal or administrative\nliability (including any disciplinary action) of the witness for\nknowingly making a statement that is false or misleading.\n\n(3) Without limiting subsection (2) of this section, section 12A does\nnot apply to the liability of the witness for an offence against\nsection 137.1, 137.2, 144.1 or 145.1 of the Criminal Code.\nDesignated publication restrictions\n\n(4) Section 12A does not apply to proceedings against the witness for\ncontravening a designated publication restriction.\nNote:\nFor designated publication restriction, see section 8.\nAssistance related to witness’ conduct\n\n(5) To avoid doubt, if the assistance provided relates to the witness’\nown conduct, section 12A does not affect the witness’ liability for\nthe conduct.\n\n\nProtection of disclosers and witnesses  Part 2\nProtections  Division 1\n\nSection 13\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nSubdivision B—Protection from reprisals"
    },
