      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.27",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Detriment includes (without limitation) any of the following:\n\n(a) dismissal of an employee;\n\n(b) injury of an employee in his or her employment;\n\n(c) alteration of an employee’s position to his or her\ndisadvantage;\n\n(d) discrimination between an employee and other employees of\nthe same employer;\n\n(e) harassment or intimidation of a person;\n\n(f) harm or injury to a person, including psychological harm;\n\n(g) damage to a person’s property;\n\n(h) damage to a person’s reputation;",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Detriment includes (without limitation) any of the following:\n\n(a) dismissal of an employee;\n\n(b) injury of an employee in his or her employment;\n\n(c) alteration of an employee’s position to his or her\ndisadvantage;\n\n(d) discrimination between an employee and other employees of\nthe same employer;\n\n(e) harassment or intimidation of a person;\n\n(f) harm or injury to a person, including psychological harm;\n\n(g) damage to a person’s property;\n\n(h) damage to a person’s reputation;",
