      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2) must not make an order under paragraph (1)(b) if the\nrespondent’s employer establishes that it took reasonable\nprecautions, and exercised due diligence, to avoid the reprisal.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2) must not make an order under paragraph (1)(b) if the\nrespondent’s employer establishes that it took reasonable\nprecautions, and exercised due diligence, to avoid the reprisal.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-14"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-14-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-14-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-14-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-14-ss-2-logic-ltl-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7b4bfbb7217216f5aabc5995b79db55c897aa29e583b0884bb6f1cedbf3ad68d",
      "skos:note": "Federal Court must not make an order under paragraph (1)(b) if the respondent's employer establishes that it took reasonable precautions and exercised due diligence to avoid reprisal."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-14-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "14(2) Compensation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2) must not make an order under paragraph (1)(b) if the\nrespondent’s employer establishes that it took reasonable\nprecautions, and exercised due diligence, to avoid the reprisal."
    },
