    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-15-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15 Injunctions, apologies and other orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-15-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.29",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 2) is satisfied, on the application of a person\n(the applicant), that another person (the respondent) took or is\ntaking a reprisal against the applicant, the Court may make any or\nall of the following orders:\n\n(a) an order granting an injunction, on such terms as the Court\nthinks appropriate:\n\n(i) restraining the respondent from taking the reprisal; or\n\n(ii) if the reprisal involves refusing or failing to do\nsomething—requiring the respondent to do that thing;\n\n(b) an order requiring the respondent to apologise to the\napplicant for taking the reprisal;\n\n(c) any other order the Court thinks appropriate.\n\n(2) If the Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 2) has power under subsection (1) to grant an\ninjunction restraining a person from engaging in particular\nconduct, or requiring a person to do anything, the Court may make\nany other orders (including granting an injunction) that it thinks\nappropriate against any other person who has:\n\n(a) aided, abetted, counselled or procured the conduct against the\napplicant; or\n\n(b) induced the conduct against the applicant, whether through\nthreats or promises or otherwise; or",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 2) is satisfied, on the application of a person\n(the applicant), that another person (the respondent) took or is\ntaking a reprisal against the applicant, the Court may make any or\nall of the following orders:\n\n(a) an order granting an injunction, on such terms as the Court\nthinks appropriate:\n\n(i) restraining the respondent from taking the reprisal; or\n\n(ii) if the reprisal involves refusing or failing to do\nsomething—requiring the respondent to do that thing;\n\n(b) an order requiring the respondent to apologise to the\napplicant for taking the reprisal;\n\n(c) any other order the Court thinks appropriate.\n\n(2) If the Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 2) has power under subsection (1) to grant an\ninjunction restraining a person from engaging in particular\nconduct, or requiring a person to do anything, the Court may make\nany other orders (including granting an injunction) that it thinks\nappropriate against any other person who has:\n\n(a) aided, abetted, counselled or procured the conduct against the\napplicant; or\n\n(b) induced the conduct against the applicant, whether through\nthreats or promises or otherwise; or",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-15-3-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-15-3-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "41ef16c379cf712cd84165a531cffad7b1449bac83e2989e3a35913712c6ba72"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-15-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15 Injunctions, apologies and other orders",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 29,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 2) is satisfied, on the application of a person\n(the applicant), that another person (the respondent) took or is\ntaking a reprisal against the applicant, the Court may make any or\nall of the following orders:\n\n(a) an order granting an injunction, on such terms as the Court\nthinks appropriate:\n\n(i) restraining the respondent from taking the reprisal; or\n\n(ii) if the reprisal involves refusing or failing to do\nsomething—requiring the respondent to do that thing;\n\n(b) an order requiring the respondent to apologise to the\napplicant for taking the reprisal;\n\n(c) any other order the Court thinks appropriate.\n\n(2) If the Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 2) has power under subsection (1) to grant an\ninjunction restraining a person from engaging in particular\nconduct, or requiring a person to do anything, the Court may make\nany other orders (including granting an injunction) that it thinks\nappropriate against any other person who has:\n\n(a) aided, abetted, counselled or procured the conduct against the\napplicant; or\n\n(b) induced the conduct against the applicant, whether through\nthreats or promises or otherwise; or"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-15-3-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15(1) Injunctions, apologies and other orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-15-3-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.29",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 2) is satisfied, on the application of a person\n(the applicant), that another person (the respondent) took or is\ntaking a reprisal against the applicant, the Court may make any or\nall of the following orders:\n\n(a) an order granting an injunction, on such terms as the Court\nthinks appropriate:\n\n(i) restraining the respondent from taking the reprisal; or\n\n(ii) if the reprisal involves refusing or failing to do\nsomething—requiring the respondent to do that thing;\n\n(b) an order requiring the respondent to apologise to the\napplicant for taking the reprisal;\n\n(c) any other order the Court thinks appropriate.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 2) is satisfied, on the application of a person\n(the applicant), that another person (the respondent) took or is\ntaking a reprisal against the applicant, the Court may make any or\nall of the following orders:\n\n(a) an order granting an injunction, on such terms as the Court\nthinks appropriate:\n\n(i) restraining the respondent from taking the reprisal; or\n\n(ii) if the reprisal involves refusing or failing to do\nsomething—requiring the respondent to do that thing;\n\n(b) an order requiring the respondent to apologise to the\napplicant for taking the reprisal;\n\n(c) any other order the Court thinks appropriate.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-15-3"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-15-3-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-15-3-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "31792bc887fe80927f0d899f6611ca9903467b5e4efb98236ccb62f84ce4915f",
      "skos:note": "Restraining respondent from taking reprisal or requiring them to do something."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-15-3-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15(1) Injunctions, apologies and other orders",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 29,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 2) is satisfied, on the application of a person\n(the applicant), that another person (the respondent) took or is\ntaking a reprisal against the applicant, the Court may make any or\nall of the following orders:\n\n(a) an order granting an injunction, on such terms as the Court\nthinks appropriate:\n\n(i) restraining the respondent from taking the reprisal; or\n\n(ii) if the reprisal involves refusing or failing to do\nsomething—requiring the respondent to do that thing;\n\n(b) an order requiring the respondent to apologise to the\napplicant for taking the reprisal;\n\n(c) any other order the Court thinks appropriate."
    },
