    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-15-3-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15(2) Injunctions, apologies and other orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-15-3-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.29",
      "values:originalText": "(2) If the Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 2) has power under subsection (1) to grant an\ninjunction restraining a person from engaging in particular\nconduct, or requiring a person to do anything, the Court may make\nany other orders (including granting an injunction) that it thinks\nappropriate against any other person who has:\n\n(a) aided, abetted, counselled or procured the conduct against the\napplicant; or\n\n(b) induced the conduct against the applicant, whether through\nthreats or promises or otherwise; or",
      "skos:definition": "(2) If the Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 2) has power under subsection (1) to grant an\ninjunction restraining a person from engaging in particular\nconduct, or requiring a person to do anything, the Court may make\nany other orders (including granting an injunction) that it thinks\nappropriate against any other person who has:\n\n(a) aided, abetted, counselled or procured the conduct against the\napplicant; or\n\n(b) induced the conduct against the applicant, whether through\nthreats or promises or otherwise; or",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-15-3"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
