    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-16",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "16 Reinstatement",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-16"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "If the Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 2) is satisfied, on the application of a person\n(the applicant), that:\n\n(a) another person (the respondent) has taken, or is taking, a\nreprisal against the applicant; and\n\n(b) the applicant is or was employed in a particular position with\nthe respondent; and\n\n(c) the reprisal wholly or partly consists, or consisted, of the\nrespondent terminating, or purporting to terminate, the\napplicant’s employment;\nthe Court may order that the applicant be reinstated in that position\nor a position at a comparable level.",
      "skos:definition": "If the Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 2) is satisfied, on the application of a person\n(the applicant), that:\n\n(a) another person (the respondent) has taken, or is taking, a\nreprisal against the applicant; and\n\n(b) the applicant is or was employed in a particular position with\nthe respondent; and\n\n(c) the reprisal wholly or partly consists, or consisted, of the\nrespondent terminating, or purporting to terminate, the\napplicant’s employment;\nthe Court may order that the applicant be reinstated in that position\nor a position at a comparable level.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-16-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-16-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-16-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-16-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-16-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-16-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a20c0b4f48cc32e67719c55d1e0398e66fb9c7b72886722dbce75fb285d1ab3e",
      "skos:note": "Reinstatement obligation for applicant if respondent takes reprisal against them."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-16",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "16 Reinstatement",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "If the Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of\nAustralia (Division 2) is satisfied, on the application of a person\n(the applicant), that:\n\n(a) another person (the respondent) has taken, or is taking, a\nreprisal against the applicant; and\n\n(b) the applicant is or was employed in a particular position with\nthe respondent; and\n\n(c) the reprisal wholly or partly consists, or consisted, of the\nrespondent terminating, or purporting to terminate, the\napplicant’s employment;\nthe Court may order that the applicant be reinstated in that position\nor a position at a comparable level."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-16-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-16"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-16-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to reinstate applicant if conditions are met.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The respondent has taken reprisal against the applicant.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The applicant must be reinstated."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-16-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "during",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Reinstatement is contingent on reprisal during employment.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The applicant was employed by the respondent.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The applicant must be reinstated if the reprisal occurred during employment."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-16-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "until",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Reinstatement is contingent on termination of reprisal.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The respondent has terminated the applicant's employment.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The applicant must be reinstated if the reprisal terminates."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-16-logic-diffusion-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "if",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Reinstatement is contingent on specific conditions being met.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The respondent has taken reprisal against the applicant.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The applicant must be reinstated if the conditions are met."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-16-logic-cogai-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "hasProperty",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Reinstatement is a property of the respondent's actions.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The respondent has taken reprisal against the applicant.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The respondent has the property of reinstating the applicant."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-17",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "17 Multiple orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-17"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "The Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2) may make orders under sections 14, 15 and 16 in\nrespect of the same conduct.\n18  Costs only if proceedings instituted vexatiously etc.\n\n(1) In proceedings (including an appeal) in a court in relation to a\nmatter arising under section 14, 15 or 16, the applicant for an order\nunder that section must not be ordered by the court to pay costs\nincurred by another party to the proceedings, except in accordance\nwith subsection (2).\n\n(2) The applicant may be ordered to pay the costs only if:\n\n(a) the court is satisfied that the applicant instituted the\nproceedings vexatiously or without reasonable cause; or\n\n\nProtection of disclosers and witnesses  Part 2\nProtections  Division 1\n\nSection 19\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the court is satisfied that the applicant’s unreasonable act or\nomission caused the other party to incur the costs.",
      "skos:definition": "The Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2) may make orders under sections 14, 15 and 16 in\nrespect of the same conduct.\n18  Costs only if proceedings instituted vexatiously etc.\n\n(1) In proceedings (including an appeal) in a court in relation to a\nmatter arising under section 14, 15 or 16, the applicant for an order\nunder that section must not be ordered by the court to pay costs\nincurred by another party to the proceedings, except in accordance\nwith subsection (2).\n\n(2) The applicant may be ordered to pay the costs only if:\n\n(a) the court is satisfied that the applicant instituted the\nproceedings vexatiously or without reasonable cause; or\n\n\nProtection of disclosers and witnesses  Part 2\nProtections  Division 1\n\nSection 19\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the court is satisfied that the applicant’s unreasonable act or\nomission caused the other party to incur the costs.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-17-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-17-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5daf9df5d801d6e8ae79032ba68f7489f00fd1db250a5c14f097ec666d846a26"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-17",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "17 Multiple orders",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "The Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2) may make orders under sections 14, 15 and 16 in\nrespect of the same conduct.\n18  Costs only if proceedings instituted vexatiously etc.\n\n(1) In proceedings (including an appeal) in a court in relation to a\nmatter arising under section 14, 15 or 16, the applicant for an order\nunder that section must not be ordered by the court to pay costs\nincurred by another party to the proceedings, except in accordance\nwith subsection (2).\n\n(2) The applicant may be ordered to pay the costs only if:\n\n(a) the court is satisfied that the applicant instituted the\nproceedings vexatiously or without reasonable cause; or\n\n\nProtection of disclosers and witnesses  Part 2\nProtections  Division 1\n\nSection 19\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the court is satisfied that the applicant’s unreasonable act or\nomission caused the other party to incur the costs."
    },
    {
