    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-26",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26 Meaning of public interest disclosure",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-26"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.39",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A disclosure of information is a public interest disclosure if:\n\n(a) the disclosure is made by a person (the discloser) who is, or\nhas been, a public official; and\n\n(b) the recipient of the information is a person of the kind\nreferred to in column 2 of an item of the following table; and\n\n(c) all the further requirements set out in column 3 of that item\nare met.\n\nPublic interest disclosures\nItem\nColumn 1\nType of\ndisclosure\nColumn 2\nRecipient\nColumn 3\nFurther requirements\nInternal\ndisclosure\nAn authorised\ninternal\nrecipient, or a\nsupervisor of\nthe discloser\n(a) The information tends to show, or the\ndiscloser believes on reasonable\ngrounds that the information tends to\nshow, one or more instances of\ndisclosable conduct.\n(b) The disclosure is not made in the\ncourse of performing the discloser’s\nordinary functions as a public official.\nExternal\ndisclosure\nAny person\nother than a\nforeign public\nofficial\n(a) The information tends to show, or the\ndiscloser believes on reasonable\ngrounds that the information tends to\nshow, one or more instances of\ndisclosable conduct.\n(b) On a previous occasion, the discloser\nmade an internal disclosure of\ninformation that consisted of, or\nincluded, the information now\ndisclosed.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A disclosure of information is a public interest disclosure if:\n\n(a) the disclosure is made by a person (the discloser) who is, or\nhas been, a public official; and\n\n(b) the recipient of the information is a person of the kind\nreferred to in column 2 of an item of the following table; and\n\n(c) all the further requirements set out in column 3 of that item\nare met.\n\nPublic interest disclosures\nItem\nColumn 1\nType of\ndisclosure\nColumn 2\nRecipient\nColumn 3\nFurther requirements\nInternal\ndisclosure\nAn authorised\ninternal\nrecipient, or a\nsupervisor of\nthe discloser\n(a) The information tends to show, or the\ndiscloser believes on reasonable\ngrounds that the information tends to\nshow, one or more instances of\ndisclosable conduct.\n(b) The disclosure is not made in the\ncourse of performing the discloser’s\nordinary functions as a public official.\nExternal\ndisclosure\nAny person\nother than a\nforeign public\nofficial\n(a) The information tends to show, or the\ndiscloser believes on reasonable\ngrounds that the information tends to\nshow, one or more instances of\ndisclosable conduct.\n(b) On a previous occasion, the discloser\nmade an internal disclosure of\ninformation that consisted of, or\nincluded, the information now\ndisclosed.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-26-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-26-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-26-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-26-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-26-logic-argumentation-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-26-logic-diffusion-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-26-logic-cogai-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "63c3b05c7f8319d36ea8fd37e4fefcaac4f86a20fe5fb3dcb90b11c9554f2648",
      "skos:note": "Disclosure of information is a public interest disclosure if certain conditions are met."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-26",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26 Meaning of public interest disclosure",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 39,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A disclosure of information is a public interest disclosure if:\n\n(a) the disclosure is made by a person (the discloser) who is, or\nhas been, a public official; and\n\n(b) the recipient of the information is a person of the kind\nreferred to in column 2 of an item of the following table; and\n\n(c) all the further requirements set out in column 3 of that item\nare met.\n\nPublic interest disclosures\nItem\nColumn 1\nType of\ndisclosure\nColumn 2\nRecipient\nColumn 3\nFurther requirements\nInternal\ndisclosure\nAn authorised\ninternal\nrecipient, or a\nsupervisor of\nthe discloser\n(a) The information tends to show, or the\ndiscloser believes on reasonable\ngrounds that the information tends to\nshow, one or more instances of\ndisclosable conduct.\n(b) The disclosure is not made in the\ncourse of performing the discloser’s\nordinary functions as a public official.\nExternal\ndisclosure\nAny person\nother than a\nforeign public\nofficial\n(a) The information tends to show, or the\ndiscloser believes on reasonable\ngrounds that the information tends to\nshow, one or more instances of\ndisclosable conduct.\n(b) On a previous occasion, the discloser\nmade an internal disclosure of\ninformation that consisted of, or\nincluded, the information now\ndisclosed."
    },
