    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-29",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29 Meaning of disclosable conduct",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-29"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.44",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Disclosable conduct is conduct of a kind mentioned in the\nfollowing table that is conduct:\n\n(a) engaged in by an agency; or\n\n(b) engaged in by a public official, in connection with his or her\nposition as a public official; or\n\n(c) engaged in by a contracted service provider for a\nCommonwealth contract, in connection with entering into, or\ngiving effect to, that contract.\n\n\nProtection of disclosers and witnesses  Part 2\nPublic interest disclosures  Division 2\n\nSection 29\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nDisclosable conduct\nItem\nKinds of disclosable conduct\nConduct that contravenes a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a\nTerritory.\nConduct, in a foreign country, that contravenes a law that:\n(a) is in force in the foreign country; and\n(b) is applicable to the agency, public official or contracted service provider;\nand\n(c) corresponds to a law in force in the Australian Capital Territory.\nConduct that:\n(a) perverts, or is engaged in for the purpose of perverting, or attempting to\npervert, the course of justice; or\n(b) involves, or is engaged in for the purpose of, corruption of any other\nkind.\nConduct that constitutes maladministration, including conduct that:\n(a) is based, in whole or in part, on improper motives; or\n(b) is unreasonable, unjust or oppressive; or\n(c) is negligent.\nConduct that is an abuse of public trust.\nConduct that is:\n(a) fabrication, falsification, plagiarism, or deception, in relation to:\n(i) proposing scientific research; or\n(ii) carrying out scientific research; or\n(iii) reporting the results of scientific research; or\n(b) misconduct relating to scientific analysis, scientific evaluation or the\ngiving of scientific advice.\nConduct that results in the wastage of:\n(a) relevant money (within the meaning of the Public Governance,\nPerformance and Accountability Act 2013); or\n(b) relevant property (within the meaning of that Act); or\n(c) money of a prescribed authority; or\n(d) property of a prescribed authority.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Disclosable conduct is conduct of a kind mentioned in the\nfollowing table that is conduct:\n\n(a) engaged in by an agency; or\n\n(b) engaged in by a public official, in connection with his or her\nposition as a public official; or\n\n(c) engaged in by a contracted service provider for a\nCommonwealth contract, in connection with entering into, or\ngiving effect to, that contract.\n\n\nProtection of disclosers and witnesses  Part 2\nPublic interest disclosures  Division 2\n\nSection 29\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nDisclosable conduct\nItem\nKinds of disclosable conduct\nConduct that contravenes a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a\nTerritory.\nConduct, in a foreign country, that contravenes a law that:\n(a) is in force in the foreign country; and\n(b) is applicable to the agency, public official or contracted service provider;\nand\n(c) corresponds to a law in force in the Australian Capital Territory.\nConduct that:\n(a) perverts, or is engaged in for the purpose of perverting, or attempting to\npervert, the course of justice; or\n(b) involves, or is engaged in for the purpose of, corruption of any other\nkind.\nConduct that constitutes maladministration, including conduct that:\n(a) is based, in whole or in part, on improper motives; or\n(b) is unreasonable, unjust or oppressive; or\n(c) is negligent.\nConduct that is an abuse of public trust.\nConduct that is:\n(a) fabrication, falsification, plagiarism, or deception, in relation to:\n(i) proposing scientific research; or\n(ii) carrying out scientific research; or\n(iii) reporting the results of scientific research; or\n(b) misconduct relating to scientific analysis, scientific evaluation or the\ngiving of scientific advice.\nConduct that results in the wastage of:\n(a) relevant money (within the meaning of the Public Governance,\nPerformance and Accountability Act 2013); or\n(b) relevant property (within the meaning of that Act); or\n(c) money of a prescribed authority; or\n(d) property of a prescribed authority.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-29-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-29-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-29-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-29-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-29-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-29-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4918bf6e80aa24257cc8067e462693aadb24c1a4b4b76207a3a38ce13de95454",
      "skos:note": "Disclosable conduct includes various types of misconduct and abuse of public trust."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-29",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "29 Meaning of disclosable conduct",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 44,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Disclosable conduct is conduct of a kind mentioned in the\nfollowing table that is conduct:\n\n(a) engaged in by an agency; or\n\n(b) engaged in by a public official, in connection with his or her\nposition as a public official; or\n\n(c) engaged in by a contracted service provider for a\nCommonwealth contract, in connection with entering into, or\ngiving effect to, that contract.\n\n\nProtection of disclosers and witnesses  Part 2\nPublic interest disclosures  Division 2\n\nSection 29\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nDisclosable conduct\nItem\nKinds of disclosable conduct\nConduct that contravenes a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a\nTerritory.\nConduct, in a foreign country, that contravenes a law that:\n(a) is in force in the foreign country; and\n(b) is applicable to the agency, public official or contracted service provider;\nand\n(c) corresponds to a law in force in the Australian Capital Territory.\nConduct that:\n(a) perverts, or is engaged in for the purpose of perverting, or attempting to\npervert, the course of justice; or\n(b) involves, or is engaged in for the purpose of, corruption of any other\nkind.\nConduct that constitutes maladministration, including conduct that:\n(a) is based, in whole or in part, on improper motives; or\n(b) is unreasonable, unjust or oppressive; or\n(c) is negligent.\nConduct that is an abuse of public trust.\nConduct that is:\n(a) fabrication, falsification, plagiarism, or deception, in relation to:\n(i) proposing scientific research; or\n(ii) carrying out scientific research; or\n(iii) reporting the results of scientific research; or\n(b) misconduct relating to scientific analysis, scientific evaluation or the\ngiving of scientific advice.\nConduct that results in the wastage of:\n(a) relevant money (within the meaning of the Public Governance,\nPerformance and Accountability Act 2013); or\n(b) relevant property (within the meaning of that Act); or\n(c) money of a prescribed authority; or\n(d) property of a prescribed authority."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-29-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
