    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-29a-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibition",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits personal work-related conduct.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Public officials must not engage in conduct that has implications for another official.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Personal work-related conduct is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-29a-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Imposes an obligation on public officials to avoid personal work-related conduct.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Public officials must not engage in conduct that has implications for another official.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Public officials have an obligation to avoid personal work-related conduct."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-29a-logic-alleninterval-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Overlaps",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Personal work-related conduct overlaps with the second official's employment or functions.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The second official's employment or functions are relevant to personal work-related conduct.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Personal work-related conduct overlaps with the second official's employment or functions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-29a-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibition",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits bullying or harassment as personal work-related conduct.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Bullying or harassment is an example of personal work-related conduct.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Bullying or harassment is prohibited as personal work-related conduct."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-29a-logic-deontic-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibition",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits the transfer or promotion of another official as personal work-related conduct.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The transfer or promotion of another official is an example of personal work-related conduct.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The transfer or promotion of another official is prohibited as personal work-related conduct."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-30",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "30 Officers or employees of a contracted service provider",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-30"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.48",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, if an individual is a public official\nbecause the individual:\n\n(a) is an officer or employee of a contracted service provider for\na Commonwealth contract; and\n\n(b) provides services for the purposes (whether direct or indirect)\nof the Commonwealth contract;\nthe individual does not engage in conduct in connection with his or\nher position as such a public official unless the conduct is in\nconnection with entering into, or giving effect to, the contract.\n\n(2) A contracted service provider for a Commonwealth contract is:\n\n(a) a person who:\n\n(i) is a party to the Commonwealth contract; and\n\n(ii) is responsible for the provision of goods or services\nunder the Commonwealth contract; or\n\n(b) a person who:\n\n(i) is a party to a contract (the subcontract) with a person\nwho is a contracted service provider for the\nCommonwealth contract under paragraph (a) (or under a\nprevious application of this paragraph); and\n\n(ii) is responsible under the subcontract for the provision of\ngoods or services for the purposes (whether direct or\nindirect) of the Commonwealth contract.\n\n(3) A Commonwealth contract is a contract:\n\n(a) to which the Commonwealth or an agency is a party; and\n\n\nProtection of disclosers and witnesses  Part 2\nPublic interest disclosures  Division 2\n\nSection 31\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) under which goods or services are to be, or were to be,\nprovided:\n\n(i) to the Commonwealth or an agency; or\n\n(ii) for or on behalf of the Commonwealth or an agency,\nand in connection with the performance of its functions\nor the exercise of its powers.\n\n(4) However, a Commonwealth contract does not include a grant\ncovered by an instrument made under section 105C of the Public\nGovernance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013\n(instruments relating to grants).\n31  Disagreements with government policies etc.\n\nTo avoid doubt, conduct is not disclosable conduct if it relates only\nto:\n\n(a) a policy or proposed policy of the Commonwealth\nGovernment; or\n\n(b) action that has been, is being, or is proposed to be, taken by:\n\n(i) a Minister; or\n\n(ii) the Speaker of the House of Representatives; or\n\n(iii) the President of the Senate; or\n\n(c) amounts, purposes or priorities of expenditure or proposed\nexpenditure relating to such a policy or proposed policy, or\nsuch action or proposed action;\nwith which a person disagrees.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, if an individual is a public official\nbecause the individual:\n\n(a) is an officer or employee of a contracted service provider for\na Commonwealth contract; and\n\n(b) provides services for the purposes (whether direct or indirect)\nof the Commonwealth contract;\nthe individual does not engage in conduct in connection with his or\nher position as such a public official unless the conduct is in\nconnection with entering into, or giving effect to, the contract.\n\n(2) A contracted service provider for a Commonwealth contract is:\n\n(a) a person who:\n\n(i) is a party to the Commonwealth contract; and\n\n(ii) is responsible for the provision of goods or services\nunder the Commonwealth contract; or\n\n(b) a person who:\n\n(i) is a party to a contract (the subcontract) with a person\nwho is a contracted service provider for the\nCommonwealth contract under paragraph (a) (or under a\nprevious application of this paragraph); and\n\n(ii) is responsible under the subcontract for the provision of\ngoods or services for the purposes (whether direct or\nindirect) of the Commonwealth contract.\n\n(3) A Commonwealth contract is a contract:\n\n(a) to which the Commonwealth or an agency is a party; and\n\n\nProtection of disclosers and witnesses  Part 2\nPublic interest disclosures  Division 2\n\nSection 31\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) under which goods or services are to be, or were to be,\nprovided:\n\n(i) to the Commonwealth or an agency; or\n\n(ii) for or on behalf of the Commonwealth or an agency,\nand in connection with the performance of its functions\nor the exercise of its powers.\n\n(4) However, a Commonwealth contract does not include a grant\ncovered by an instrument made under section 105C of the Public\nGovernance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013\n(instruments relating to grants).\n31  Disagreements with government policies etc.\n\nTo avoid doubt, conduct is not disclosable conduct if it relates only\nto:\n\n(a) a policy or proposed polic",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-30-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-30-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-30-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-30-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5d72ef3b8acd47ff02f94144c74b7c31efc05f5f90871c7eedd1526178807149"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-30",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "30 Officers or employees of a contracted service provider",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 48,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, if an individual is a public official\nbecause the individual:\n\n(a) is an officer or employee of a contracted service provider for\na Commonwealth contract; and\n\n(b) provides services for the purposes (whether direct or indirect)\nof the Commonwealth contract;\nthe individual does not engage in conduct in connection with his or\nher position as such a public official unless the conduct is in\nconnection with entering into, or giving effect to, the contract.\n\n(2) A contracted service provider for a Commonwealth contract is:\n\n(a) a person who:\n\n(i) is a party to the Commonwealth contract; and\n\n(ii) is responsible for the provision of goods or services\nunder the Commonwealth contract; or\n\n(b) a person who:\n\n(i) is a party to a contract (the subcontract) with a person\nwho is a contracted service provider for the\nCommonwealth contract under paragraph (a) (or under a\nprevious application of this paragraph); and\n\n(ii) is responsible under the subcontract for the provision of\ngoods or services for the purposes (whether direct or\nindirect) of the Commonwealth contract.\n\n(3) A Commonwealth contract is a contract:\n\n(a) to which the Commonwealth or an agency is a party; and\n\n\nProtection of disclosers and witnesses  Part 2\nPublic interest disclosures  Division 2\n\nSection 31\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) under which goods or services are to be, or were to be,\nprovided:\n\n(i) to the Commonwealth or an agency; or\n\n(ii) for or on behalf of the Commonwealth or an agency,\nand in connection with the performance of its functions\nor the exercise of its powers.\n\n(4) However, a Commonwealth contract does not include a grant\ncovered by an instrument made under section 105C of the Public\nGovernance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013\n(instruments relating to grants).\n31  Disagreements with government policies etc.\n\nTo avoid doubt, conduct is not disclosable conduct if it relates only\nto:\n\n(a) a policy or proposed policy of the Commonwealth\nGovernment; or\n\n(b) action that has been, is being, or is proposed to be, taken by:\n\n(i) a Minister; or\n\n(ii) the Speaker of the House of Representatives; or\n\n(iii) the President of the Senate; or\n\n(c) amounts, purposes or priorities of expenditure or proposed\nexpenditure relating to such a policy or proposed policy, or\nsuch action or proposed action;\nwith which a person disagrees."
    },
