      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.49",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Despite section 29, conduct is not disclosable conduct if it is:\n\n(a) conduct of a judicial officer; or\n\n(b) conduct of:\n\n(i) the chief executive officer of a court; or\n\n(ii) a member of the staff of the chief executive officer of a\ncourt;",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Despite section 29, conduct is not disclosable conduct if it is:\n\n(a) conduct of a judicial officer; or\n\n(b) conduct of:\n\n(i) the chief executive officer of a court; or\n\n(ii) a member of the staff of the chief executive officer of a\ncourt;",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-32-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-32-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "57a4c675827dc422d698ad83fb6bd5a81dcd019d01340dda3c34579ae9e47c70",
      "skos:note": "Conduct of judicial officers and certain court staff is not disclosable conduct."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-32",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32 Conduct connected with courts or Commonwealth tribunals",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 49,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Despite section 29, conduct is not disclosable conduct if it is:\n\n(a) conduct of a judicial officer; or\n\n(b) conduct of:\n\n(i) the chief executive officer of a court; or\n\n(ii) a member of the staff of the chief executive officer of a\ncourt;"
    },
