    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-34",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "34 Meaning of authorised internal recipient",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-34"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.51",
      "values:originalText": "The following table sets out who is an authorised internal\nrecipient of a disclosure of information that the discloser believes\non reasonable grounds may concern one or more instances of\ndisclosable conduct.\n\nAuthorised internal recipients\nItem\nColumn 1\nIf the conduct with\nwhich the disclosure is\nconcerned relates to:\nColumn 2\nAn authorised officer of any of the following\nagencies is an authorised internal recipient of\nthe disclosure:\nan agency (other than an\nintelligence agency, the\n(a) in any case—that agency;\n(b) the agency to which the discloser belongs, or",
      "skos:definition": "The following table sets out who is an authorised internal\nrecipient of a disclosure of information that the discloser believes\non reasonable grounds may concern one or more instances of\ndisclosable conduct.\n\nAuthorised internal recipients\nItem\nColumn 1\nIf the conduct with\nwhich the disclosure is\nconcerned relates to:\nColumn 2\nAn authorised officer of any of the following\nagencies is an authorised internal recipient of\nthe disclosure:\nan agency (other than an\nintelligence agency, the\n(a) in any case—that agency;\n(b) the agency to which the discloser belongs, or",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-34-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cd334c575e65e728ed416cc5af38c776ca9633d86bded69b749e2a01e2a9b391",
      "skos:note": "Defines who is an authorized internal recipient of a disclosure."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-34",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "34 Meaning of authorised internal recipient",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 51,
      "values:originalText": "The following table sets out who is an authorised internal\nrecipient of a disclosure of information that the discloser believes\non reasonable grounds may concern one or more instances of\ndisclosable conduct.\n\nAuthorised internal recipients\nItem\nColumn 1\nIf the conduct with\nwhich the disclosure is\nconcerned relates to:\nColumn 2\nAn authorised officer of any of the following\nagencies is an authorised internal recipient of\nthe disclosure:\nan agency (other than an\nintelligence agency, the\n(a) in any case—that agency;\n(b) the agency to which the discloser belongs, or"
    },
    {
