    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-44a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44A Allocation of disclosure—decision not to allocate",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-44a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.63",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if an authorised officer of an agency decides,\nunder paragraph 43(3)(b), not to allocate a disclosure to any\nagency.\nReferral of conduct for investigation under another law or power\n\n(2) If the authorised officer is satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that the\nconduct disclosed would be more appropriately investigated under\nanother law or power, the authorised officer must, as soon as\nreasonably practicable, take reasonable steps to refer the conduct\ndisclosed, or to facilitate its referral, for investigation under the\nother law or power.\nNotice of decision not to allocate disclosure\n\n(3) As soon as reasonably practicable after making the decision not to\nallocate the disclosure, the authorised officer of the agency must:\n\n(a) if reasonably practicable, give written notice to the discloser\nof:\n\n(i) the decision not to allocate the disclosure, and the\nreasons for the decision; and\n\n(ii) if the authorised officer has taken action, or proposes to\ntake action, under subsection (2)—the details of the\naction taken or proposed; and",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if an authorised officer of an agency decides,\nunder paragraph 43(3)(b), not to allocate a disclosure to any\nagency.\nReferral of conduct for investigation under another law or power\n\n(2) If the authorised officer is satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that the\nconduct disclosed would be more appropriately investigated under\nanother law or power, the authorised officer must, as soon as\nreasonably practicable, take reasonable steps to refer the conduct\ndisclosed, or to facilitate its referral, for investigation under the\nother law or power.\nNotice of decision not to allocate disclosure\n\n(3) As soon as reasonably practicable after making the decision not to\nallocate the disclosure, the authorised officer of the agency must:\n\n(a) if reasonably practicable, give written notice to the discloser\nof:\n\n(i) the decision not to allocate the disclosure, and the\nreasons for the decision; and\n\n(ii) if the authorised officer has taken action, or proposes to\ntake action, under subsection (2)—the details of the\naction taken or proposed; and",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-44a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-44a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-44a-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000"
    },
    {
