      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.65",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The authorised officer must, as soon as reasonably practicable,\ngive written notice of the matters in subsection (3) to:\n\n(a) the Ombudsman (unless paragraph (b) of this subsection\napplies); or\n\n(b) the IGIS, if the disclosure concerns conduct relating to:\n\n(i) an intelligence agency; or\n\n(ii) the IGIS; or\n\n(iii) AUSTRAC, the Department of Home Affairs or the\nAustralian Federal Police in relation to that agency’s\nintelligence functions.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The authorised officer must, as soon as reasonably practicable,\ngive written notice of the matters in subsection (3) to:\n\n(a) the Ombudsman (unless paragraph (b) of this subsection\napplies); or\n\n(b) the IGIS, if the disclosure concerns conduct relating to:\n\n(i) an intelligence agency; or\n\n(ii) the IGIS; or\n\n(iii) AUSTRAC, the Department of Home Affairs or the\nAustralian Federal Police in relation to that agency’s\nintelligence functions.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-44b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-44b-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-44b-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8405774ff34e1f4e9f66e42040e7d1db2269dbb05385f195bd5fa5081c507048",
      "skos:note": "Authorised officer must give written notice to Ombudsman or IGIS under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-44b-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44B(2) Non-allocation of disclosure subject to stop action direction",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 65,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The authorised officer must, as soon as reasonably practicable,\ngive written notice of the matters in subsection (3) to:\n\n(a) the Ombudsman (unless paragraph (b) of this subsection\napplies); or\n\n(b) the IGIS, if the disclosure concerns conduct relating to:\n\n(i) an intelligence agency; or\n\n(ii) the IGIS; or\n\n(iii) AUSTRAC, the Department of Home Affairs or the\nAustralian Federal Police in relation to that agency’s\nintelligence functions."
    },
    {
