      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) the anticipated time remaining before the investigation is completed;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-46",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "46 Simplified outline",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-46"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.68",
      "values:originalText": "The following is a simplified outline of this Division:\nThe principal officer of the allocated agency must investigate the\ndisclosure, and prepare a report, within a set time and in\naccordance with the requirements of this Division.\nHowever, a stop action direction under the NACC Act may prevent\nthe investigation of some or all of the disclosure.\nThe principal officer may decide not to investigate in particular\ncircumstances in which an investigation is unjustified, or if the\nagency is an investigative agency that can investigate without\nusing this Act.\nNote:\nThe way a disclosure is investigated (or a refusal to investigate a\ndisclosure) may be the subject of a complaint to the Ombudsman\nunder the Ombudsman Act 1976, or (in the case of an intelligence\nagency, or AUSTRAC, the Department of Home Affairs or the\nAustralian Federal Police in relation to that agency’s intelligence\nfunctions) to the IGIS under the Inspector-General of Intelligence and\nSecurity Act 1986.",
      "skos:definition": "The following is a simplified outline of this Division:\nThe principal officer of the allocated agency must investigate the\ndisclosure, and prepare a report, within a set time and in\naccordance with the requirements of this Division.\nHowever, a stop action direction under the NACC Act may prevent\nthe investigation of some or all of the disclosure.\nThe principal officer may decide not to investigate in particular\ncircumstances in which an investigation is unjustified, or if the\nagency is an investigative agency that can investigate without\nusing this Act.\nNote:\nThe way a disclosure is investigated (or a refusal to investigate a\ndisclosure) may be the subject of a complaint to the Ombudsman\nunder the Ombudsman Act 1976, or (in the case of an intelligence\nagency, or AUSTRAC, the Department of Home Affairs or the\nAustralian Federal Police in relation to that agency’s intelligence\nfunctions) to the IGIS under the Inspector-General of Intelligence and\nSecurity Act 1986.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-46-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-46-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "295f88de4add498ca6731a96a7a8c93c2ead21c27598ed16890aad7fae0039b2",
      "skos:note": "Agency must investigate disclosure within set time and in accordance with Division requirements."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-46",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "46 Simplified outline",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 68,
      "values:originalText": "The following is a simplified outline of this Division:\nThe principal officer of the allocated agency must investigate the\ndisclosure, and prepare a report, within a set time and in\naccordance with the requirements of this Division.\nHowever, a stop action direction under the NACC Act may prevent\nthe investigation of some or all of the disclosure.\nThe principal officer may decide not to investigate in particular\ncircumstances in which an investigation is unjustified, or if the\nagency is an investigative agency that can investigate without\nusing this Act.\nNote:\nThe way a disclosure is investigated (or a refusal to investigate a\ndisclosure) may be the subject of a complaint to the Ombudsman\nunder the Ombudsman Act 1976, or (in the case of an intelligence\nagency, or AUSTRAC, the Department of Home Affairs or the\nAustralian Federal Police in relation to that agency’s intelligence\nfunctions) to the IGIS under the Inspector-General of Intelligence and\nSecurity Act 1986."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-46-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-46"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-46-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Agency must investigate disclosure within set time.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-47",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "47 Principal officer must investigate disclosures",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-47"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.68",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The principal officer of an agency must investigate a disclosure if\nthe disclosure is allocated to the agency under Division 1.\n\n(2) Investigate, in relation to a disclosure, means investigate (or\nreinvestigate) whether there are one or more instances of\ndisclosable conduct. The disclosable conduct may relate to:\n\n(a) the information that is disclosed; or\n\n(b) information obtained in the course of the investigation,\nunless the principal officer conducting the investigation is\n\n\nInvestigations  Part 3\nThe obligation to investigate disclosures  Division 2\n\nSection 48\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nsatisfied on reasonable grounds that such information is\ntangential or remote to the disclosure.\nNote 1:\nA disclosure may be reinvestigated in response to a recommendation\nby the Ombudsman or the IGIS under section 55.\nNote 2:\nIf the principal officer of the agency does not investigate information\nmentioned in paragraph (b) in the investigation of the disclosure, the\nprincipal officer may choose to investigate the information disclosed\notherwise than under this Act.\n\n(3) For the purposes of subsection (2), an investigation (or\nreinvestigation) may include consideration of whether a different\ninvestigation (or reinvestigation) should be conducted by the\nagency, or another body, under another law or power.\nStop action directions under the NACC Act\n\n(4) This section has effect subject to any stop action direction under\nthe NACC Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The principal officer of an agency must investigate a disclosure if\nthe disclosure is allocated to the agency under Division 1.\n\n(2) Investigate, in relation to a disclosure, means investigate (or\nreinvestigate) whether there are one or more instances of\ndisclosable conduct. The disclosable conduct may relate to:\n\n(a) the information that is disclosed; or\n\n(b) information obtained in the course of the investigation,\nunless the principal officer conducting the investigation is\n\n\nInvestigations  Part 3\nThe obligation to investigate disclosures  Division 2\n\nSection 48\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nsatisfied on reasonable grounds that such information is\ntangential or remote to the disclosure.\nNote 1:\nA disclosure may be reinvestigated in response to a recommendation\nby the Ombudsman or the IGIS under section 55.\nNote 2:\nIf the principal officer of the agency does not investigate information\nmentioned in paragraph (b) in the investigation of the disclosure, the\nprincipal officer may choose to investigate the information disclosed\notherwise than under this Act.\n\n(3) For the purposes of subsection (2), an investigation (or\nreinvestigation) may include consideration of whether a different\ninvestigation (or reinvestigation) should be conducted by the\nagency, or another body, under another law or power.\nStop action directions under the NACC Act\n\n(4) This section has effect subject to any stop action direction under\nthe NACC Act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-47-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-47-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-47-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-47-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ada7c778691a71876fd605ba736ef890e39cc48a0779c6f307fe23777cfec7a1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-47",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "47 Principal officer must investigate disclosures",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 68,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The principal officer of an agency must investigate a disclosure if\nthe disclosure is allocated to the agency under Division 1.\n\n(2) Investigate, in relation to a disclosure, means investigate (or\nreinvestigate) whether there are one or more instances of\ndisclosable conduct. The disclosable conduct may relate to:\n\n(a) the information that is disclosed; or\n\n(b) information obtained in the course of the investigation,\nunless the principal officer conducting the investigation is\n\n\nInvestigations  Part 3\nThe obligation to investigate disclosures  Division 2\n\nSection 48\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nsatisfied on reasonable grounds that such information is\ntangential or remote to the disclosure.\nNote 1:\nA disclosure may be reinvestigated in response to a recommendation\nby the Ombudsman or the IGIS under section 55.\nNote 2:\nIf the principal officer of the agency does not investigate information\nmentioned in paragraph (b) in the investigation of the disclosure, the\nprincipal officer may choose to investigate the information disclosed\notherwise than under this Act.\n\n(3) For the purposes of subsection (2), an investigation (or\nreinvestigation) may include consideration of whether a different\ninvestigation (or reinvestigation) should be conducted by the\nagency, or another body, under another law or power.\nStop action directions under the NACC Act\n\n(4) This section has effect subject to any stop action direction under\nthe NACC Act."
    },
    {
