    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-48",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "48 Discretion not to investigate",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-48"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.69",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Despite section 47, the principal officer of the agency may decide\nnot to investigate the disclosure, or (if the investigation has started)\nnot to investigate the disclosure further, if:\n\n(a) the discloser is not, and has not been, a public official; or\n\n(c) the information does not, to any extent, concern serious\ndisclosable conduct; or\n\n(d) the disclosure is frivolous or vexatious; or\n\n(e) the information is the same, or substantially the same, as\ninformation previously disclosed under this Act, and:\n\n(i) a decision was previously made under this subsection\nnot to investigate the earlier disclosure, or not to\ninvestigate the earlier disclosure further; or\n\n(ii) the earlier disclosure has been, or is being, investigated\nas a disclosure investigation; or\n\n(f) the conduct disclosed, or substantially the same conduct, is\nbeing investigated under another law or power, and the\nprincipal officer is satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that it",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Despite section 47, the principal officer of the agency may decide\nnot to investigate the disclosure, or (if the investigation has started)\nnot to investigate the disclosure further, if:\n\n(a) the discloser is not, and has not been, a public official; or\n\n(c) the information does not, to any extent, concern serious\ndisclosable conduct; or\n\n(d) the disclosure is frivolous or vexatious; or\n\n(e) the information is the same, or substantially the same, as\ninformation previously disclosed under this Act, and:\n\n(i) a decision was previously made under this subsection\nnot to investigate the earlier disclosure, or not to\ninvestigate the earlier disclosure further; or\n\n(ii) the earlier disclosure has been, or is being, investigated\nas a disclosure investigation; or\n\n(f) the conduct disclosed, or substantially the same conduct, is\nbeing investigated under another law or power, and the\nprincipal officer is satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that it",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-48-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-48-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "96357b2d22f1fc52ad845c4464d2daf57a76f011ce8d2c82ef0bf102b14eef02",
      "skos:note": "Principal officer may decide not to investigate disclosure under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-48",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "48 Discretion not to investigate",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 69,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Despite section 47, the principal officer of the agency may decide\nnot to investigate the disclosure, or (if the investigation has started)\nnot to investigate the disclosure further, if:\n\n(a) the discloser is not, and has not been, a public official; or\n\n(c) the information does not, to any extent, concern serious\ndisclosable conduct; or\n\n(d) the disclosure is frivolous or vexatious; or\n\n(e) the information is the same, or substantially the same, as\ninformation previously disclosed under this Act, and:\n\n(i) a decision was previously made under this subsection\nnot to investigate the earlier disclosure, or not to\ninvestigate the earlier disclosure further; or\n\n(ii) the earlier disclosure has been, or is being, investigated\nas a disclosure investigation; or\n\n(f) the conduct disclosed, or substantially the same conduct, is\nbeing investigated under another law or power, and the\nprincipal officer is satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that it"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-48-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-48"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
