      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.72",
      "values:originalText": "(4A) The principal officer must, as soon as reasonably practicable, give\nwritten notice to the discloser if the principal officer investigates,\nor further investigates, a disclosure that is no longer subject to a\nstop action direction under the NACC Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(4A) The principal officer must, as soon as reasonably practicable, give\nwritten notice to the discloser if the principal officer investigates,\nor further investigates, a disclosure that is no longer subject to a\nstop action direction under the NACC Act.",
