    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-50a-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "50A(4) Notification to Ombudsman or IGIS about investigation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-50a-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.74",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If a stop action direction under the NACC Act prevents the\nprincipal officer of the agency from investigating, or further\ninvestigating, the disclosure under this Division, the principal\nofficer must, as soon as reasonably practicable, give written notice\nof the stop action direction to:\n\n(a) the Ombudsman (unless paragraph (b) applies); or\n\n(b) the IGIS, if the disclosure concerns conduct relating to:\n\n(i) an intelligence agency; or\n\n(ii) the IGIS; or\n\n(iii) AUSTRAC, the Department of Home Affairs or the\nAustralian Federal Police in relation to that agency’s\nintelligence functions.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If a stop action direction under the NACC Act prevents the\nprincipal officer of the agency from investigating, or further\ninvestigating, the disclosure under this Division, the principal\nofficer must, as soon as reasonably practicable, give written notice\nof the stop action direction to:\n\n(a) the Ombudsman (unless paragraph (b) applies); or\n\n(b) the IGIS, if the disclosure concerns conduct relating to:\n\n(i) an intelligence agency; or\n\n(ii) the IGIS; or\n\n(iii) AUSTRAC, the Department of Home Affairs or the\nAustralian Federal Police in relation to that agency’s\nintelligence functions.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-50a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-50a-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-50a-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2e0d8e1a88ce9be540c7769f9603b280b1bcc0c21af5fcf40fba62066476df1a",
      "skos:note": "Principal officer must give written notice of stop action direction to Ombudsman or IGIS.",
      "dc:description": "written notice"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-50a-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "50A(4) Notification to Ombudsman or IGIS about investigation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 74,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If a stop action direction under the NACC Act prevents the\nprincipal officer of the agency from investigating, or further\ninvestigating, the disclosure under this Division, the principal\nofficer must, as soon as reasonably practicable, give written notice\nof the stop action direction to:\n\n(a) the Ombudsman (unless paragraph (b) applies); or\n\n(b) the IGIS, if the disclosure concerns conduct relating to:\n\n(i) an intelligence agency; or\n\n(ii) the IGIS; or\n\n(iii) AUSTRAC, the Department of Home Affairs or the\nAustralian Federal Police in relation to that agency’s\nintelligence functions."
    },
