    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-53",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "53 Conduct of investigations under this Division",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-53"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.78",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An investigation under this Division by the principal officer of an\nagency is to be conducted as the person thinks fit.\n\n(2) The principal officer may, for the purposes of the investigation,\nobtain information from such persons, and make such inquiries, as\nthe principal officer thinks fit.\n\n\nInvestigations  Part 3\nThe obligation to investigate disclosures  Division 2\n\nSection 54\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(3) Despite subsections (1) and (2), in conducting the investigation, the\nprincipal officer must comply with any standards in force under\nsection 74.\n\n(4) Despite subsections (1) and (2), the principal officer must act in\naccordance with any rules relating to fraud that are made for the\npurposes of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013, to the extent that:\n\n(a) the investigation relates to one or more instances of fraud;\nand\n\n(b) those rules are not inconsistent with this Act (apart from\nsubsections (1) and (2)).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An investigation under this Division by the principal officer of an\nagency is to be conducted as the person thinks fit.\n\n(2) The principal officer may, for the purposes of the investigation,\nobtain information from such persons, and make such inquiries, as\nthe principal officer thinks fit.\n\n\nInvestigations  Part 3\nThe obligation to investigate disclosures  Division 2\n\nSection 54\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(3) Despite subsections (1) and (2), in conducting the investigation, the\nprincipal officer must comply with any standards in force under\nsection 74.\n\n(4) Despite subsections (1) and (2), the principal officer must act in\naccordance with any rules relating to fraud that are made for the\npurposes of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013, to the extent that:\n\n(a) the investigation relates to one or more instances of fraud;\nand\n\n(b) those rules are not inconsistent with this Act (apart from\nsubsections (1) and (2)).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-53-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-53-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-53-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-53-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bda3adf14dde7765974eb6f07d28511e9d3d1b7ff2fb4240f34eb1acd31c896b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-53",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "53 Conduct of investigations under this Division",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 78,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An investigation under this Division by the principal officer of an\nagency is to be conducted as the person thinks fit.\n\n(2) The principal officer may, for the purposes of the investigation,\nobtain information from such persons, and make such inquiries, as\nthe principal officer thinks fit.\n\n\nInvestigations  Part 3\nThe obligation to investigate disclosures  Division 2\n\nSection 54\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(3) Despite subsections (1) and (2), in conducting the investigation, the\nprincipal officer must comply with any standards in force under\nsection 74.\n\n(4) Despite subsections (1) and (2), the principal officer must act in\naccordance with any rules relating to fraud that are made for the\npurposes of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013, to the extent that:\n\n(a) the investigation relates to one or more instances of fraud;\nand\n\n(b) those rules are not inconsistent with this Act (apart from\nsubsections (1) and (2))."
    },
