    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-55",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55 The Ombudsman and the IGIS—recommendations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-55"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.80",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if the Ombudsman or the IGIS (the relevant\ninvestigative agency):\n\n(a) under subsection 44(2)—is notified of the allocation of a\ndisclosure to an agency; or\n\n(b) under subsection 44A(3)—is notified of a decision not to\nallocate a disclosure to any agency; or\n\n(c) under section 50A—is notified by the principal officer of an\nagency of a decision not to investigate a disclosure under",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if the Ombudsman or the IGIS (the relevant\ninvestigative agency):\n\n(a) under subsection 44(2)—is notified of the allocation of a\ndisclosure to an agency; or\n\n(b) under subsection 44A(3)—is notified of a decision not to\nallocate a disclosure to any agency; or\n\n(c) under section 50A—is notified by the principal officer of an\nagency of a decision not to investigate a disclosure under",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-55-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-55-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "04247aafcd2a112373be40c7c5519cbcda2888b59bcb24b80070ef3e8acdf988",
      "skos:note": "Notification of allocation or non-allocation of disclosure to an agency"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-55",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55 The Ombudsman and the IGIS—recommendations",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 80,
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if the Ombudsman or the IGIS (the relevant\ninvestigative agency):\n\n(a) under subsection 44(2)—is notified of the allocation of a\ndisclosure to an agency; or\n\n(b) under subsection 44A(3)—is notified of a decision not to\nallocate a disclosure to any agency; or\n\n(c) under section 50A—is notified by the principal officer of an\nagency of a decision not to investigate a disclosure under"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-55-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-55"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-55-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "has",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Notification obligation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "IGIS is notified of allocation or non-allocation",
      "cml:conclusionText": "IGIS must investigate disclosure"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-56",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "56 Disclosure to a member of an Australian police force",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-56"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.82",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if, in the course of a disclosure investigation,\nthe person (the investigator) conducting the investigation suspects\non reasonable grounds that information (the relevant information),\nconsisting of all or part of any of the following information, is\nevidence of the commission of an offence against a law of the\nCommonwealth, a State or a Territory:\n\n(a) the information disclosed;\n\n\nInvestigations  Part 3\nMiscellaneous  Division 3\n\nSection 56\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) any other information obtained in the course of the\ninvestigation.\nPower to give information to police\n\n(2) The investigator may give the relevant information to a member of\nan Australian police force responsible for the investigation of the\noffence.\nDuty to give information to police\n\n(3) However, if the investigator suspects on reasonable grounds that\nthe offence is punishable by imprisonment for life or by\nimprisonment for a period of at least 2 years, the investigator must\ngive the relevant information to a member of an Australian police\nforce responsible for the investigation of the offence.\n\n(4) However, subsection (3) does not apply:\n\n(a) if the investigator believes on reasonable grounds that the\nagency to which the investigator belongs has the capacity and\nthe appropriate skills and resources needed:\n\n(i) to investigate the commission of the offence; and\n\n(ii) to meet the requirements of the Commonwealth\nDirector of Public Prosecutions in gathering evidence\nand preparing briefs of evidence in relation to the\ncommission of the offence; or\n\n(b) if the investigator suspects on reasonable grounds that the\nrelevant information raises a corruption issue (within the\nmeaning of the National Anti-Corruption Commission Act\n2022) and:\n\n(i) the corruption issue has been referred under that Act to\nthe person or agency mentioned in subsection (4A); or\n\n(ii) that person or agency is already aware of the issue.\n\n(4A) For the purposes of paragraph (4)(b), the person or agency is:\n\n(a) the National Anti-Corruption Commissioner; or\n\n(b) the IGIS, if the corruption issue concerns:\n\n(i) an intelligence agency; or",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if, in the course of a disclosure investigation,\nthe person (the investigator) conducting the investigation suspects\non reasonable grounds that information (the relevant information),\nconsisting of all or part of any of the following information, is\nevidence of the commission of an offence against a law of the\nCommonwealth, a State or a Territory:\n\n(a) the information disclosed;\n\n\nInvestigations  Part 3\nMiscellaneous  Division 3\n\nSection 56\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) any other information obtained in the course of the\ninvestigation.\nPower to give information to police\n\n(2) The investigator may give the relevant information to a member of\nan Australian police force responsible for the investigation of the\noffence.\nDuty to give information to police\n\n(3) However, if the investigator suspects on reasonable grounds that\nthe offence is punishable by imprisonment for life or by\nimprisonment for a period of at least 2 years, the investigator must\ngive the relevant information to a member of an Australian police\nforce responsible for the investigation of the offence.\n\n(4) However, subsection (3) does not apply:\n\n(a) if the investigator believes on reasonable grounds that the\nagency to which the investigator belongs has the capacity and\nthe appropriate skills and resources needed:\n\n(i) to investigate the commission of the offence; and\n\n(ii) to meet the requirements of the Commonwealth\nDirector of Public Prosecutions in gathering evidence\nand preparing briefs of evidence in relation to the\ncommission of the offence; or\n\n(b) if the investigator suspects on reasonable grounds that the\nrelevant information raises a corruption issue (within the\nmeaning of the National Anti-Corruption Commission Act\n2022) and:\n\n(i) the corruption issue has been referred under that Act to\nthe person or agency mentioned in subsection (4A); or\n\n(ii) that person or agency is already aware of the issue.\n\n(4A) For the purposes ",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-56-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-56-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-56-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-56-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-56-ss-4a"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-56",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "56 Disclosure to a member of an Australian police force",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 82,
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if, in the course of a disclosure investigation,\nthe person (the investigator) conducting the investigation suspects\non reasonable grounds that information (the relevant information),\nconsisting of all or part of any of the following information, is\nevidence of the commission of an offence against a law of the\nCommonwealth, a State or a Territory:\n\n(a) the information disclosed;\n\n\nInvestigations  Part 3\nMiscellaneous  Division 3\n\nSection 56\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) any other information obtained in the course of the\ninvestigation.\nPower to give information to police\n\n(2) The investigator may give the relevant information to a member of\nan Australian police force responsible for the investigation of the\noffence.\nDuty to give information to police\n\n(3) However, if the investigator suspects on reasonable grounds that\nthe offence is punishable by imprisonment for life or by\nimprisonment for a period of at least 2 years, the investigator must\ngive the relevant information to a member of an Australian police\nforce responsible for the investigation of the offence.\n\n(4) However, subsection (3) does not apply:\n\n(a) if the investigator believes on reasonable grounds that the\nagency to which the investigator belongs has the capacity and\nthe appropriate skills and resources needed:\n\n(i) to investigate the commission of the offence; and\n\n(ii) to meet the requirements of the Commonwealth\nDirector of Public Prosecutions in gathering evidence\nand preparing briefs of evidence in relation to the\ncommission of the offence; or\n\n(b) if the investigator suspects on reasonable grounds that the\nrelevant information raises a corruption issue (within the\nmeaning of the National Anti-Corruption Commission Act\n2022) and:\n\n(i) the corruption issue has been referred under that Act to\nthe person or agency mentioned in subsection (4A); or\n\n(ii) that person or agency is already aware of the issue.\n\n(4A) For the purposes of paragraph (4)(b), the person or agency is:\n\n(a) the National Anti-Corruption Commissioner; or\n\n(b) the IGIS, if the corruption issue concerns:\n\n(i) an intelligence agency; or"
    },
