      "cml:conclusionText": "Disclosure must be made within a reasonable timeframe"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-60a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "60A Additional obligations of supervisors",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-60a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.88",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a public official (the discloser) discloses information to a\nsupervisor of the official; and\n\n(b) the supervisor has reasonable grounds to believe that the\ninformation concerns, or could concern, one or more\ninstances of disclosable conduct; and\n\n(c) the supervisor is not an authorised officer of the agency to\nwhich the supervisor belongs.\n\n\nAdministrative matters  Part 4\nAdditional obligations and functions  Division 1\n\nSection 61\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nObligation to explain matters to discloser\n\n(2) The supervisor must:\n\n(a) inform the discloser that the disclosure could be treated as an\ninternal disclosure for the purposes of this Act; and\n\n(b) explain to the discloser the procedures under this Act for\nsuch a disclosure to be:\n\n(i) given to an authorised officer; and\n\n(ii) allocated to the discloser’s agency or another agency;\nand\n\n(iii) investigated by the principal officer of that agency; and\n\n(c) advise the individual about the circumstances (if any) in\nwhich a public interest disclosure must be referred to an\nagency, or other person or body, under another law of the\nCommonwealth; and\n\n(d) explain to the discloser the civil and criminal protections this\nAct provides to protect disclosers, and those providing\nassistance in relation to such disclosures, from reprisals.\nObligation to give information to an authorised officer\n\n(3) The supervisor must, as soon as reasonably practicable after the\ndisclosure is made, give the information to an authorised officer of\nthe agency.",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a public official (the discloser) discloses information to a\nsupervisor of the official; and\n\n(b) the supervisor has reasonable grounds to believe that the\ninformation concerns, or could concern, one or more\ninstances of disclosable conduct; and\n\n(c) the supervisor is not an authorised officer of the agency to\nwhich the supervisor belongs.\n\n\nAdministrative matters  Part 4\nAdditional obligations and functions  Division 1\n\nSection 61\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nObligation to explain matters to discloser\n\n(2) The supervisor must:\n\n(a) inform the discloser that the disclosure could be treated as an\ninternal disclosure for the purposes of this Act; and\n\n(b) explain to the discloser the procedures under this Act for\nsuch a disclosure to be:\n\n(i) given to an authorised officer; and\n\n(ii) allocated to the discloser’s agency or another agency;\nand\n\n(iii) investigated by the principal officer of that agency; and\n\n(c) advise the individual about the circumstances (if any) in\nwhich a public interest disclosure must be referred to an\nagency, or other person or body, under another law of the\nCommonwealth; and\n\n(d) explain to the discloser the civil and criminal protections this\nAct provides to protect disclosers, and those providing\nassistance in relation to such disclosures, from reprisals.\nObligation to give information to an authorised officer\n\n(3) The supervisor must, as soon as reasonably practicable after the\ndisclosure is made, give the information to an authorised officer of\nthe agency.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
