    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-62",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "62 Additional functions of the Ombudsman",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-62"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.90",
      "values:originalText": "The functions of the Ombudsman include:\n\n(a) assisting:\n\n(i) principal officers of agencies (other than intelligence\nagencies or the IGIS); and\n\n(ii) authorised officers of agencies (other than intelligence\nagencies or the IGIS); and\n\n(iii) public officials who belong to agencies (other than\nintelligence agencies or the IGIS); and\n\n(iv) former public officials who belonged to agencies (other\nthan intelligence agencies or the IGIS);\n\nin relation to the operation of this Act; and\n\n(b) conducting educational and awareness programs relating to\nthis Act, to the extent to which this Act relates to:\n\n(i) agencies (other than intelligence agencies or the IGIS);\nand\n\n(ii) public officials who belong to agencies (other than\nintelligence agencies or the IGIS); and\n\n(iii) former public officials who belonged to agencies (other\nthan intelligence agencies or the IGIS); and\n\n(c) assisting the IGIS in relation to the performance of the\nfunctions conferred on the IGIS by this Act.\nNote:\nSection 5A of the Ombudsman Act 1976 extends the Ombudsman’s\nfunctions to cover disclosures of information that have been, or are\nrequired to be, allocated under section 43 of this Act (whether or not\nthey are allocated to the Ombudsman), if the disclosable conduct with\nwhich the information is concerned relates to an agency other than an\nintelligence agency or the IGIS.\n\n\nAdministrative matters  Part 4\nAdditional obligations and functions  Division 1\n\nSection 63\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "The functions of the Ombudsman include:\n\n(a) assisting:\n\n(i) principal officers of agencies (other than intelligence\nagencies or the IGIS); and\n\n(ii) authorised officers of agencies (other than intelligence\nagencies or the IGIS); and\n\n(iii) public officials who belong to agencies (other than\nintelligence agencies or the IGIS); and\n\n(iv) former public officials who belonged to agencies (other\nthan intelligence agencies or the IGIS);\n\nin relation to the operation of this Act; and\n\n(b) conducting educational and awareness programs relating to\nthis Act, to the extent to which this Act relates to:\n\n(i) agencies (other than intelligence agencies or the IGIS);\nand\n\n(ii) public officials who belong to agencies (other than\nintelligence agencies or the IGIS); and\n\n(iii) former public officials who belonged to agencies (other\nthan intelligence agencies or the IGIS); and\n\n(c) assisting the IGIS in relation to the performance of the\nfunctions conferred on the IGIS by this Act.\nNote:\nSection 5A of the Ombudsman Act 1976 extends the Ombudsman’s\nfunctions to cover disclosures of information that have been, or are\nrequired to be, allocated under section 43 of this Act (whether or not\nthey are allocated to the Ombudsman), if the disclosable conduct with\nwhich the information is concerned relates to an agency other than an\nintelligence agency or the IGIS.\n\n\nAdministrative matters  Part 4\nAdditional obligations and functions  Division 1\n\nSection 63\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-62-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-62-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a8161ef38f12f4c7ebbec3a637dc80b792959a93d338f7765aa0ae5c429b6d89",
      "skos:note": "The Ombudsman must assist principal officers, authorised officers, public officials, and former public officials in relation to the operation of this Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-62",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "62 Additional functions of the Ombudsman",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 90,
      "values:originalText": "The functions of the Ombudsman include:\n\n(a) assisting:\n\n(i) principal officers of agencies (other than intelligence\nagencies or the IGIS); and\n\n(ii) authorised officers of agencies (other than intelligence\nagencies or the IGIS); and\n\n(iii) public officials who belong to agencies (other than\nintelligence agencies or the IGIS); and\n\n(iv) former public officials who belonged to agencies (other\nthan intelligence agencies or the IGIS);\n\nin relation to the operation of this Act; and\n\n(b) conducting educational and awareness programs relating to\nthis Act, to the extent to which this Act relates to:\n\n(i) agencies (other than intelligence agencies or the IGIS);\nand\n\n(ii) public officials who belong to agencies (other than\nintelligence agencies or the IGIS); and\n\n(iii) former public officials who belonged to agencies (other\nthan intelligence agencies or the IGIS); and\n\n(c) assisting the IGIS in relation to the performance of the\nfunctions conferred on the IGIS by this Act.\nNote:\nSection 5A of the Ombudsman Act 1976 extends the Ombudsman’s\nfunctions to cover disclosures of information that have been, or are\nrequired to be, allocated under section 43 of this Act (whether or not\nthey are allocated to the Ombudsman), if the disclosable conduct with\nwhich the information is concerned relates to an agency other than an\nintelligence agency or the IGIS.\n\n\nAdministrative matters  Part 4\nAdditional obligations and functions  Division 1\n\nSection 63\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-62-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-62"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-62-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The Ombudsman has a duty to assist certain individuals.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-63",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "63 Additional functions of the IGIS",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-63"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.91",
      "values:originalText": "The functions of the IGIS include:\n\n(a) assisting:\n\n(i) principal officers of intelligence agencies; and\n\n(ii) authorised officers of intelligence agencies or the IGIS;\nand\n\n(iii) public officials who belong to intelligence agencies or\nthe IGIS; and\n\n(iv) former public officials who belonged to intelligence\nagencies or the IGIS;\n\nin relation to the operation of this Act; and\n\n(aa) assisting, in relation to the intelligence functions of\nAUSTRAC, the Department of Home Affairs or the\nAustralian Federal Police:\n\n(i) principal officers of that agency; and\n\n(ii) authorised officers of that agency; and\n\n(iii) public officials who belong to that agency; and\n\n(iv) former public officials who belonged to that agency;\n\nin relation to the operation of this Act; and\n\n(b) conducting educational and awareness programs relating to\nthis Act, to the extent to which this Act relates to:\n\n(i) intelligence agencies; and\n\n(ii) public officials who belong to intelligence agencies; and\n\n(iii) former public officials who belonged to intelligence\nagencies; and\n\n(ba) conducting educational and awareness programs relating to\nthis Act, in relation to the intelligence functions of\nAUSTRAC, the Department of Home Affairs or the\nAustralian Federal Police, to the extent to which this Act\nrelates to:\n\n(i) that agency; and\n\n(ii) public officials who belong to that agency; and\n\n(iii) former public officials who belonged to that agency;\nand",
      "skos:definition": "The functions of the IGIS include:\n\n(a) assisting:\n\n(i) principal officers of intelligence agencies; and\n\n(ii) authorised officers of intelligence agencies or the IGIS;\nand\n\n(iii) public officials who belong to intelligence agencies or\nthe IGIS; and\n\n(iv) former public officials who belonged to intelligence\nagencies or the IGIS;\n\nin relation to the operation of this Act; and\n\n(aa) assisting, in relation to the intelligence functions of\nAUSTRAC, the Department of Home Affairs or the\nAustralian Federal Police:\n\n(i) principal officers of that agency; and\n\n(ii) authorised officers of that agency; and\n\n(iii) public officials who belong to that agency; and\n\n(iv) former public officials who belonged to that agency;\n\nin relation to the operation of this Act; and\n\n(b) conducting educational and awareness programs relating to\nthis Act, to the extent to which this Act relates to:\n\n(i) intelligence agencies; and\n\n(ii) public officials who belong to intelligence agencies; and\n\n(iii) former public officials who belonged to intelligence\nagencies; and\n\n(ba) conducting educational and awareness programs relating to\nthis Act, in relation to the intelligence functions of\nAUSTRAC, the Department of Home Affairs or the\nAustralian Federal Police, to the extent to which this Act\nrelates to:\n\n(i) that agency; and\n\n(ii) public officials who belong to that agency; and\n\n(iii) former public officials who belonged to that agency;\nand",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-63-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-63-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6f17b56e5e28a8a606977192db84cd5ae0e238f6859d991fd3ed5ba651b1be5f",
      "skos:note": "The IGIS must assist principal officers of intelligence agencies and public officials who belong to intelligence agencies in relation to the operation of this Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-63",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "63 Additional functions of the IGIS",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 91,
      "values:originalText": "The functions of the IGIS include:\n\n(a) assisting:\n\n(i) principal officers of intelligence agencies; and\n\n(ii) authorised officers of intelligence agencies or the IGIS;\nand\n\n(iii) public officials who belong to intelligence agencies or\nthe IGIS; and\n\n(iv) former public officials who belonged to intelligence\nagencies or the IGIS;\n\nin relation to the operation of this Act; and\n\n(aa) assisting, in relation to the intelligence functions of\nAUSTRAC, the Department of Home Affairs or the\nAustralian Federal Police:\n\n(i) principal officers of that agency; and\n\n(ii) authorised officers of that agency; and\n\n(iii) public officials who belong to that agency; and\n\n(iv) former public officials who belonged to that agency;\n\nin relation to the operation of this Act; and\n\n(b) conducting educational and awareness programs relating to\nthis Act, to the extent to which this Act relates to:\n\n(i) intelligence agencies; and\n\n(ii) public officials who belong to intelligence agencies; and\n\n(iii) former public officials who belonged to intelligence\nagencies; and\n\n(ba) conducting educational and awareness programs relating to\nthis Act, in relation to the intelligence functions of\nAUSTRAC, the Department of Home Affairs or the\nAustralian Federal Police, to the extent to which this Act\nrelates to:\n\n(i) that agency; and\n\n(ii) public officials who belong to that agency; and\n\n(iii) former public officials who belonged to that agency;\nand"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-63-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
