    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-67",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "67 Secrecy—legal practitioners",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-67"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.94",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person has obtained information in the person’s capacity\nas the recipient of a legal practitioner disclosure; and\n\n\nAdministrative matters  Part 4\nTreatment of information  Division 2\n\nSection 67\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the person:\n\n(i) discloses the information to another person; or\n\n(ii) uses the information.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years or 120 penalty units, or both.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) the disclosure or use is for the purpose of providing legal\nadvice, or professional assistance, relating to a public interest\ndisclosure (other than a legal practitioner disclosure) made,\nor proposed to be made, by the person who made the legal\npractitioner disclosure referred to in paragraph (1)(a); or\n\n(b) the information has previously been lawfully published.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to a matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person has obtained information in the person’s capacity\nas the recipient of a legal practitioner disclosure; and\n\n\nAdministrative matters  Part 4\nTreatment of information  Division 2\n\nSection 67\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the person:\n\n(i) discloses the information to another person; or\n\n(ii) uses the information.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years or 120 penalty units, or both.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) the disclosure or use is for the purpose of providing legal\nadvice, or professional assistance, relating to a public interest\ndisclosure (other than a legal practitioner disclosure) made,\nor proposed to be made, by the person who made the legal\npractitioner disclosure referred to in paragraph (1)(a); or\n\n(b) the information has previously been lawfully published.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to a matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-67-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-67-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4d8b056ab2824c54db12c84d76eec321167a8e186d5ff34a9033c663a1cfebad"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-67",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "67 Secrecy—legal practitioners",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 94,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person has obtained information in the person’s capacity\nas the recipient of a legal practitioner disclosure; and\n\n\nAdministrative matters  Part 4\nTreatment of information  Division 2\n\nSection 67\n\nPublic Interest Disclosure Act 2013\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the person:\n\n(i) discloses the information to another person; or\n\n(ii) uses the information.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years or 120 penalty units, or both.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) the disclosure or use is for the purpose of providing legal\nadvice, or professional assistance, relating to a public interest\ndisclosure (other than a legal practitioner disclosure) made,\nor proposed to be made, by the person who made the legal\npractitioner disclosure referred to in paragraph (1)(a); or\n\n(b) the information has previously been lawfully published.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to a matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-67-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "67(1) Secrecy—legal practitioners",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
