    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-67-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "67(2) Secrecy—legal practitioners",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-67-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.94",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) the disclosure or use is for the purpose of providing legal\nadvice, or professional assistance, relating to a public interest\ndisclosure (other than a legal practitioner disclosure) made,\nor proposed to be made, by the person who made the legal\npractitioner disclosure referred to in paragraph (1)(a); or\n\n(b) the information has previously been lawfully published.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to a matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) the disclosure or use is for the purpose of providing legal\nadvice, or professional assistance, relating to a public interest\ndisclosure (other than a legal practitioner disclosure) made,\nor proposed to be made, by the person who made the legal\npractitioner disclosure referred to in paragraph (1)(a); or\n\n(b) the information has previously been lawfully published.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to a matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-67"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-67-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-67-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "499da35885690be7b5e82d2ccf80d75b0d9fdd5186e045b1c6bee48f4f3cb500",
      "skos:note": "Disclosure for legal advice or professional assistance is permitted."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-67-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "67(2) Secrecy—legal practitioners",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 94,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if:\n\n(a) the disclosure or use is for the purpose of providing legal\nadvice, or professional assistance, relating to a public interest\ndisclosure (other than a legal practitioner disclosure) made,\nor proposed to be made, by the person who made the legal\npractitioner disclosure referred to in paragraph (1)(a); or\n\n(b) the information has previously been lawfully published.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to a matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code)."
    },
