    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-73",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "73 Meaning of principal officer",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-73"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.103",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, the principal officer of an agency\nmentioned in column 1 of an item in the following table is the\nperson specified in column 2 of the item.\n\nPrincipal officers of agencies\nItem\nColumn 1\nAgency\nColumn 2\nPrincipal officer\nA Department.\nThe Secretary of the Department.\nThe Australian Federal Police.\nThe Commissioner of Police (within the\nmeaning of the Australian Federal Police\nAct 1979).\nThe High Court or any court\ncreated by the Parliament.\nThe chief executive officer of the court.\nThe Office of Official\nSecretary to the\nGovernor-General\nThe Official Secretary to the\nGovernor-General.\nThe Ombudsman.\nThe Ombudsman.\nThe IGIS.\nThe IGIS.\nA prescribed authority that is\nconstituted by an individual.\nThe individual.\nAny other agency.\nWhichever of the following individuals is\napplicable:\n(a) the chief executive officer, or the head,\nhowever described, of the agency;\n(b) if another individual is ascertained in\naccordance with the PID rules—that\nother individual.\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Act:",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, the principal officer of an agency\nmentioned in column 1 of an item in the following table is the\nperson specified in column 2 of the item.\n\nPrincipal officers of agencies\nItem\nColumn 1\nAgency\nColumn 2\nPrincipal officer\nA Department.\nThe Secretary of the Department.\nThe Australian Federal Police.\nThe Commissioner of Police (within the\nmeaning of the Australian Federal Police\nAct 1979).\nThe High Court or any court\ncreated by the Parliament.\nThe chief executive officer of the court.\nThe Office of Official\nSecretary to the\nGovernor-General\nThe Official Secretary to the\nGovernor-General.\nThe Ombudsman.\nThe Ombudsman.\nThe IGIS.\nThe IGIS.\nA prescribed authority that is\nconstituted by an individual.\nThe individual.\nAny other agency.\nWhichever of the following individuals is\napplicable:\n(a) the chief executive officer, or the head,\nhowever described, of the agency;\n(b) if another individual is ascertained in\naccordance with the PID rules—that\nother individual.\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Act:",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-73-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-73-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cfe03ea6fb33d4bf72c883cec9155efb2bb1288ce3654a9aef9250c7541aebcc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-73",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
