    {
      "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-76a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "76A Six-monthly reports by the Ombudsman",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-76a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-interest-disclosure-act-2013.pdf, p.110",
      "values:originalText": "Report on period 1 July to 31 December each year\n\n(1) The Ombudsman must, as soon as practicable after the end of each\ncalendar year, prepare and give to the Minister, for presentation to\nParliament, a report on the operation of this Act during the period\nfrom 1 July to 31 December in the calendar year.\nNote:\nSee also section 34C of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901, which\ncontains extra rules about periodic reports.\n\n(2) The report must include the information covered by\nparagraphs 76(2)(a) to (d) (which deal with annual reports) in\nrelation to the period from 1 July to 31 December in the calendar\nyear.\n\n(3) Subsections 76(3) and (4) apply in relation to a report under this\nsection in the same way as they apply in relation to a report under\nsection 76.\nNote:\nSubsections 76(3) and (4) relate to the powers of the Ombudsman and\nprincipal officers of agencies in relation to the preparation of annual\nreports.",
      "skos:definition": "Report on period 1 July to 31 December each year\n\n(1) The Ombudsman must, as soon as practicable after the end of each\ncalendar year, prepare and give to the Minister, for presentation to\nParliament, a report on the operation of this Act during the period\nfrom 1 July to 31 December in the calendar year.\nNote:\nSee also section 34C of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901, which\ncontains extra rules about periodic reports.\n\n(2) The report must include the information covered by\nparagraphs 76(2)(a) to (d) (which deal with annual reports) in\nrelation to the period from 1 July to 31 December in the calendar\nyear.\n\n(3) Subsections 76(3) and (4) apply in relation to a report under this\nsection in the same way as they apply in relation to a report under\nsection 76.\nNote:\nSubsections 76(3) and (4) relate to the powers of the Ombudsman and\nprincipal officers of agencies in relation to the preparation of annual\nreports.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-76a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-76a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-interest-disclosure-act-2013-sec-76a-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "10bb1d69194c96b06a91119b406d96110bfcf83dc3d0d4b2cc73bb928fad47de"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-interest-disclosure-act-2013#sec-76a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "76A Six-monthly reports by the Ombudsman",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 110,
      "values:originalText": "Report on period 1 July to 31 December each year\n\n(1) The Ombudsman must, as soon as practicable after the end of each\ncalendar year, prepare and give to the Minister, for presentation to\nParliament, a report on the operation of this Act during the period\nfrom 1 July to 31 December in the calendar year.\nNote:\nSee also section 34C of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901, which\ncontains extra rules about periodic reports.\n\n(2) The report must include the information covered by\nparagraphs 76(2)(a) to (d) (which deal with annual reports) in\nrelation to the period from 1 July to 31 December in the calendar\nyear.\n\n(3) Subsections 76(3) and (4) apply in relation to a report under this\nsection in the same way as they apply in relation to a report under\nsection 76.\nNote:\nSubsections 76(3) and (4) relate to the powers of the Ombudsman and\nprincipal officers of agencies in relation to the preparation of annual\nreports."
    },
